{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>How long will this people provoke Me, and how long.</b> They said in the Midrash: the Holy One, blessed be He, said: I cried out two cries on your account; in the end you are destined to cry out four in the subjugation of the kingdoms — (Psalms 13:2) ״עד אנה ה׳ תשכחני נצח עד אנה תסתיר את פניך ממני״, ״עד אנה אשית עצות בנפשי יגון בלבבי יומם עד אנה ירום אויבי עלי״. I cried out 'ad matay' (how long) for the congregation; in the end you are destined to cry out (ibid. 13:3) ״ונפשי נבהלה מאד ואתה ה׳ עד מתי״." "<b>In the midst of it.</b> It does not say 'in your midst' (בקרבכם) but 'in the midst of it' (בקרבו), in the singular. By way of the plain sense (peshat): at the time when they were of one heart toward their Father in heaven." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> 'In the midst of it' — that they had no need to go out to relieve themselves, as we say (Leviticus 1:13) ״והקרב והכרעים״. And they interpreted in tractate Yoma: from the fact that Israel ate in the wilderness, it was absorbed into the limbs; if so, how do I fulfill (Deuteronomy 23:14) ״ויתד תהיה לך על אזניך״ — with the things that merchants of the nations of the world sell to them." "<b>And further.</b> There are those who say there, after they sinned: for even the things that merchants of the nations of the world would sell them were thereby neutralized (מן היה מפיגן); but after they sinned and the Holy One, blessed be He, said to them, 'I had said you should be before Me like the ministering angels, and now I burden you to go out outside the camp three parasangs,' as it is written (Numbers 33:49) ״ויחנו על הירדן מבית הישימות״, and Rabba bar bar Ḥana said: I myself saw that place and it was three parasangs."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {2 "Citation marked ויקרא א׳:י״ג in the source; 'והקרב והכרעים' is Leviticus 1:13. The reading 'מן שהיו' appears elliptical; rendered hyper-literally.", 3 "The phrase 'מן היה מפיגן' is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. Meaning likely 'it was thereby nullified/neutralized.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:16.742574579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}